  └────────┬────────┘
           │ generates
           ↓
  ┌─────────────────┐
  │  PromptPreview  │  # Shows result
  │  Display text   │
  └─────────────────┘

  ---
  🔑 Key Concepts (Simple Terms)

  React Components

  - Like functions that return HTML
  - Can receive data (props)
  - Can remember data (state)
  - Can react to changes

  State (useState)

  - Like a whiteboard that remembers things
  - When you write on it, React notices and updates the screen

  useEffect (The Watcher)

  - Like a security camera that watches specific variables
  - When those variables change, it runs a function
  - Used here to regenerate prompt when form data changes

  Props (Data Passing)

  - Like passing a note to someone
  - Parent passes data to child
  - Child cannot change the note, only read it

  TypeScript

  - Like a spellchecker for code
  - Catches mistakes before you run the app
  - Ensures the right data types are used

